meta { title = Language guide, order = 1, group = Learn }

Start with a small program, then learn how to compose functions, work with data, and send typed work to parallel workers.

The examples below describe the implemented Kalandra port. They are compiled and executed by the project test suite. This is a guide to the current language, not a promise that every historical Clio feature is available.

h2 { Follow the guide }

link { url = /docs/guide/first-program, 1. Your first program }

link { url = /docs/guide/functions, 2. Functions and pipes }

link { url = /docs/guide/collections, 3. Arrays and maps }

