h2 { Run the examples }

Use the Try in playground link on a lesson to load its exact example. Loading an example does not run it automatically. The playground has a ten-second limit and supports one source file without network access or package imports.

After installing the CLI, save a lesson's source as main.kalandra and run it:

codeblock { language = bash, "kalandra run main.kalandra --strict" }

link { url = /docs/getting-started, Install Kalandra }

link { url = /docs/guide/limits, Current limits and port status }

Source files use .kalandra and projects use kalandra.toml. Kalandra is a new beginning; Clio project formats are not supported.
